one of the main arguments i make here on  the bioneer is that physical training  and cognitive training should go hand in  hand  few characters in fiction embody this  philosophy like  deathstroke the terminator while the  explanations have been pseudo-scientific  at times  slade is generally said to be able to  think nine times faster than a normal  human  this is what allows him to go toe-to-toe  with the likes of batman and nightwing  he is a master tactician he picks up new  martial arts with ease  and he has heightened speed and decision  making in combat  and this is where things get really  interesting because if you could  increase your working memory  a core component of iq then it actually  could help you to become a better mover  and maybe even a combat prodigy this is  something that can be achieved to a more  subtle degree  with the right kind of training in this  video i will argue that anyone can  benefit from a cognitive skills training  day  in their routine here's what that should  look like inspired by the calculating  mercenary  of course if you want to see how this  might fit into a broader training  program  you could also check out my ebook and  training routine super functional  training  there's a link down below and it's  currently on discount or keep listening  and i'll tell you how this all works and  how you can design your own skills day  so working memory is your capacity to  store and manipulate information  in the short term when performing maths  for example  you use your working memory to carry  numbers or keep the question in mind  while working  this is what much of the research  focused on for years but working memory  is also what we use to store information  about the world around us  when playing sports for example we use  working memory to remember where the  other players are on the pitch  something similar occurs when you're  moving normally through space because  you can only focus on a narrow amount of  information at any given time  you therefore need to build up a picture  of the world around you that is  constantly updated  see my recent video and post on training  reflexes focus and decision making like  john wick  this way working memory can improve your  vision for driving in sports as well as  your ability to react  dynamically to changing scenes all of  this is crucial in combat  if deathstroke could hypothetically  attempt to more information at once  he might be able to maintain a more  complete picture of his current  situation  and react to small changes more rapidly  this of course would make him a far more  lethal combatant and could explain his  tactical mind  but what's more is that working memory  also helps you to move your body  and learn new skills that's motor  learning  if you've ever been taught how to punch  or how to swing a golf club you'll  likely remember being given lots of  information about how to move  when punching you need to rotate the  hips and the shoulders you need to keep  loose until the last minute  depending on the style of martial arts  you must also rotate the fist as it  travels  this is a lot to remember and that's  just the tip of the iceberg keeping all  of this in mind during the early stages  of motor learning  requires working memory and attention  this is what p fitz and m posner  described as the cognitive phase of  learning motor skills  the point at which you still need to  consciously control your movements  so if slade has a greater working memory  he can increase the awareness  of his own body and thereby move each  limb and muscle as instructed  this could help him to rapidly learn new  martial arts and to deliver more power  with each strike  and this is not hypothetical in one  study it was found that children with  greater working memories  responded better to instructions when  learning basketball shooting  learning faster and to greater effect  several more studies have shown similar  results  in one it was found that 